  <title>Bookmarks and Tags</title>

  <p>Bookmarks let you mark individual verses for quick return later. Press
  <keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>B</key></keyseq>, or use the right-click context
  menu in the <gui>Bible Text Pane</gui>, to open the bookmark dialog on the
  current verse. Bookmarks are listed in the <gui>Sidebar</gui>, where they can
  be organized into folders.</p>

  <!-- TODO: confirm exact dialog/menu wording for tag folder colors against
  source (added by commits ff96e592 #1317, a9dd210f #1336, ecbb544d #1368). -->
  <section id="xiphos-bookmark-tag-colors">
    <title>Coloring Tag Folders</title>
    <media style="image" mime="image/png" src="figures/bookmarks.png" />
    <p>Bookmark folders (also called tag folders) can now be given a color.
    Right-click a folder in the bookmark list and choose a color for it. Every
    verse bookmarked into that folder is then highlighted in the chosen color
    directly in the <gui>Bible Text Pane</gui>, giving you an at-a-glance
    picture of how your tags are distributed through a passage, similar to
    highlighting a paper Bible with different colored pens for different
    themes.</p>
    <p>A verse that belongs to more than one colored tag folder, or that also
    carries a personal annotation, is resolved consistently so that only one
    color is shown; the bookmark dialog always shows you exactly which
    folder(s) a verse belongs to.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="xiphos-bookmark-crossref-popup">
    <title>Navigating Multi-Verse References</title>
    <p>Bookmarks and cross-references that point to more than one verse (for
    example, a reference spanning several verses, or several distinct
    references bundled together) can be navigated one at a time from a popup
    menu, without first sending the whole list to the sidebar's verse list.
    Partial verse references are also resolved correctly when building this
    popup, instead of only whole-verse or whole-chapter references.</p>
  </section>

